{%- comment -%}
  data-hide-when-active: comma-separated CSS selector list. Any matching
  element anywhere on the page is hidden while the cart contains a fixed/
  selling plan (handled by hide-controller.ts), and restored otherwise.
  Wire to a section setting (e.g. section.settings.juo_hide_selectors) to make
  it merchant-configurable from the theme editor; leave blank to disable.

  native-fetch: add this boolean attribute only if the merchant's theme
  monkey-patches window.fetch (bundle apps like Kaching Bundles) and that breaks
  the cart swap. It routes just the checkout-swap cart writes (cart/clear +
  cart/add.js) through a pristine fetch from a hidden iframe. Off by default.
{%- endcomment -%}
<juo-checkout-link
  data-hide-when-active="[name='checkout'], .cart__checkout-button"
>
  {{- 'sections.cart.checkout_local_payments' | t -}}
</juo-checkout-link>
